<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Why Is the Sky Blue? — 为什么天空是蓝色的？</title>
<style>
  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

  body {
    font-family: -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, "PingFang SC", "Microsoft YaHei", sans-serif;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #87CEEB 0%, #E0F0FF 100%);
    min-height: 100vh;
    color: #1e293b;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  header {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 2.5rem 1rem 1.5rem;
  }
  header h1 {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #1e3a5f;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  header p {
    margin-top: .4rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: #475569;
  }

  /* ---- Tab bar ---- */
  .tabs {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: .5rem;
    padding: 0 1rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .tabs button {
    padding: .55rem 1.4rem;
    border: 2px solid #3b82f6;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: #fff;
    color: #3b82f6;
    font-size: .9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all .2s ease;
  }
  .tabs button:hover { background: #eff6ff; }
  .tabs button.active {
    background: #3b82f6;
    color: #fff;
  }

  /* ---- Layout ---- */
  .container {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1rem 3rem;
  }

  /* Two-column view */
  .columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .columns.single { grid-template-columns: 1fr; max-width: 740px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }

  .panel {
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 16px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.08);
    padding: 2rem 2.2rem;
    overflow: auto;
    transition: opacity .25s ease;
  }
  .panel.hidden { display: none; }

  .panel h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: #3b82f6;
    margin-bottom: .8rem;
    padding-bottom: .4rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #eff6ff;
  }
  .panel h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: #6366f1;
    margin: 1.4rem 0 .5rem;
  }
  .panel p { margin-bottom: .8rem; font-size: .92rem; }
  .panel strong { color: #1e3a5f; }
  .panel ol, .panel ul { padding-left: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: .8rem; }
  .panel li { font-size: .92rem; margin-bottom: .3rem; }

  .panel .emoji { font-size: 1.2rem; }

  /* Math blocks */
  .math {
    background: #f8fafc;
    border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: .8rem 1rem;
    margin: .8rem 0;
    font-family: "Cambria Math", "Times New Roman", Georgia, serif;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: .95rem;
    text-align: center;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  /* Divider between sections */
  .section { padding-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .section + .section { border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; padding-top: 1.5rem; }

  /* Footer */
  footer {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    font-size: .8rem;
    color: #94a3b8;
  }

  /* Responsive */
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .columns { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <h1>Why Is the Sky Blue? — 为什么天空是蓝色的？</h1>
  <p>Three explanations for three audiences — bilingual side-by-side</p>
</header>

<div class="tabs">
  <button class="active" data-view="both" onclick="setView('both')">Both / 对照</button>
  <button data-view="en" onclick="setView('en')">English Only</button>
  <button data-view="zh" onclick="setView('zh')">中文 Only</button>
</div>

<div class="container">
  <div class="columns" id="grid">

    <!-- ====== ENGLISH PANEL ====== -->
    <div class="panel" id="panel-en">

      <div class="section">
        <h2>🧒 For a 3-Year-Old</h2>
        <p>Sunlight looks white, but it's actually made of lots of rainbow colors mixed together — like red, yellow, green, and blue! When sunlight reaches Earth, it bumps into tiny tiny particles in the air (like invisible dust). The blue light bumps and bounces around the most, spreading everywhere. So when you look up, you see that bouncing blue light all over the sky. That's why the sky is blue! <span class="emoji">🌈</span></p>
      </div>

      <div class="section">
        <h2>🎒 For a High School Teenager</h2>
        <p>The sky is blue because of a phenomenon called <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong>. Sunlight appears white, but it actually contains all visible wavelengths of light — from red (~700 nm) to violet (~400 nm). When sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it collides with gas molecules (mostly nitrogen and oxygen). These molecules are much smaller than the wavelength of visible light.</p>
        <p>Shorter wavelengths (blue and violet) scatter much more strongly than longer wavelengths (red and orange). In fact, scattering intensity is inversely proportional to the fourth power of wavelength (<strong>I ∝ 1/λ⁴</strong>), so blue light scatters roughly <strong>9–10 times more</strong> than red light.</p>
        <p>But if blue scatters the most, why isn't the sky violet? Two reasons:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>The Sun emits more blue light than violet light.</li>
          <li>Our eyes are much more sensitive to blue than violet, so we perceive the scattered light as blue.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>At sunset, sunlight travels through more atmosphere, so most of the blue is scattered away before it reaches your eyes — leaving the reds and oranges you see.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="section">
        <h2>🔬 For a Physics PhD</h2>
        <p>The blue color of the sky arises from <strong>elastic scattering of sunlight by atmospheric molecules</strong>, described quantitatively by <strong>Rayleigh scattering theory</strong>. The differential scattering cross-section for a particle much smaller than the incident wavelength (ka ≪ 1) is given by:</p>
        <div class="math">dσ/dΩ = (2π⁵ α² / 3λ⁴ R²) · (1 + cos²θ)</div>
        <p>where α is the polarizability of the molecule, λ is the wavelength, and θ is the scattering angle. The <strong>λ⁻⁴ dependence</strong> means shorter wavelengths are strongly preferentially scattered — blue (~450 nm) is scattered ~5× more than green (~550 nm) and ~9× more than red (~650 nm).</p>
        <p>More rigorously, one can model the atmosphere using the <strong>Lorentz-Lorenz equation</strong> for the refractive index and compute the scattering from the fluctuations in the dielectric constant:</p>
        <div class="math">dσ/dΩ ∝ [(n² − 1) / (n² + 2)]² · 1/λ⁴</div>
        <p>For nitrogen and oxygen (the dominant atmospheric constituents), the polarizabilities yield an effective refractive index of n ≈ 1.0003, producing the observed sky radiance.</p>
        <p>The sky isn't violet despite violet's even shorter wavelength because:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Solar spectral irradiance</strong> peaks in the visible (~500 nm) and declines sharply in the UV/violet (AM1.5 spectrum).</li>
          <li><strong>Human photoreceptor response</strong> (CIE color matching functions) shows S-cone sensitivity peaks at ~420–440 nm and drops sharply below 410 nm.</li>
          <li>The <strong>ozone layer</strong> absorbs a significant portion of UV and near-UV radiation, further reducing violet contribution.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>At sunset, the increased <strong>optical path length</strong> through the atmosphere (secant law, τ<sub>eff</sub> ≈ τ₀ sec ζ where ζ is the zenith angle) leads to heavy attenuation of short wavelengths via extinction, leaving the transmitted red/orange spectrum.</p>
        <p>For a complete treatment, one would solve the <strong>radiative transfer equation</strong> through the atmosphere, incorporating Mie scattering from aerosols (which is roughly wavelength-independent and causes the whitish haze), multiple scattering events, and surface albedo contributions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ====== CHINESE PANEL ====== -->
    <div class="panel" id="panel-zh">

      <div class="section">
        <h2>🧒 给三岁小朋友</h2>
        <p>阳光看起来是白色的，但其实它是由很多彩虹颜色混在一起组成的——比如红色、黄色、绿色和蓝色！当阳光来到地球时，它会撞上空气里 tiny tiny 的小颗粒（就像看不见的灰尘）。蓝光撞得最多、弹得最欢，到处都是。所以当你抬头看时，你就能看到满天空的蓝色光弹来弹去。这就是天空是蓝色的原因！<span class="emoji">🌈</span></p>
      </div>

      <div class="section">
        <h2>🎒 给高中生</h2>
        <p>天空是蓝色的，是因为一种叫做<strong>瑞利散射</strong>的现象。阳光看起来是白色的，但其实它包含了所有可见光波长的光——从红光（约 700 nm）到紫光（约 400 nm）。当阳光进入地球大气层时，它会与气体分子（主要是氮气和氧气）发生碰撞。这些分子比可见光的波长小得多。</p>
        <p>较短的波长（蓝光和紫光）比较长的波长（红光和橙光）散射得强烈得多。实际上，散射强度与波长的四次方成反比（<strong>I ∝ 1/λ⁴</strong>），因此蓝光的散射大约是红光的 <strong>9–10 倍</strong>。</p>
        <p>但如果蓝光散射得最多，为什么天空不是紫色的呢？有两个原因：</p>
        <ol>
          <li>太阳发出的蓝光比紫光多。</li>
          <li>我们的眼睛对蓝光的敏感度远比对紫光的敏感度高，因此我们将散射光感知为蓝色。</li>
        </ol>
        <p>日落时，阳光穿过更多的大气层，所以大部分蓝光在到达你的眼睛之前就被散射掉了——留下你看到的红色和橙色。</p>
      </div>

      <div class="section">
        <h2>🔬 给物理学博士</h2>
        <p>天空的蓝色来源于<strong>大气分子对阳光的弹性散射</strong>，可用<strong>瑞利散射理论</strong>定量描述。对于远小于入射波长的粒子（ka ≪ 1），微分散射截面为：</p>
        <div class="math">dσ/dΩ = (2π⁵ α² / 3λ⁴ R²) · (1 + cos²θ)</div>
        <p>其中 α 为分子的极化率，λ 为波长，θ 为散射角。<strong>λ⁻⁴ 依赖性</strong>意味着较短波长的光被强烈优先散射——蓝光（约 450 nm）的散射约为绿光（约 550 nm）的 5 倍，约为红光（约 650 nm）的 9 倍。</p>
        <p>更严格地说，可以利用<strong>洛伦兹-洛伦茨方程</strong>对折射率建模，并从介电常数的涨落计算散射：</p>
        <div class="math">dσ/dΩ ∝ [(n² − 1) / (n² + 2)]² · 1/λ⁴</div>
        <p>对于氮气和氧气（大气的主要成分），其极化率给出有效折射率 n ≈ 1.0003，产生观测到的天空辐射亮度。</p>
        <p>尽管紫光的波长更短，但天空并非紫色，原因如下：</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>太阳光谱辐照度</strong>在可见光区域（约 500 nm）达到峰值，在紫外/紫光区域急剧下降（AM1.5 光谱）。</li>
          <li><strong>人类光感受器响应</strong>（CIE 色匹配函数）显示 S 锥细胞敏感度峰值在约 420–440 nm，并在 410 nm 以下急剧下降。</li>
          <li><strong>臭氧层</strong>吸收了相当一部分紫外线和近紫外线辐射，进一步减少了紫光的贡献。</li>
        </ul>
        <p>日落时，穿过大气的<strong>光程长度</strong>增加（正割定律，τ<sub>eff</sub> ≈ τ₀ sec ζ，其中 ζ 为天顶角），导致短波长光因消光而严重衰减，留下透射的红/橙光谱。</p>
        <p>对于完整处理，需求解穿过大气的<strong>辐射转移方程</strong>，纳入气溶胶的米氏散射（大致与波长无关，导致白色薄雾）、多次散射事件以及地表反照率贡献。</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>

<footer>Bilingual presentation — English & Simplified Chinese</footer>

<script>
function setView(view) {
  const grid  = document.getElementById('grid');
  const en    = document.getElementById('panel-en');
  const zh    = document.getElementById('panel-zh');

  en.classList.remove('hidden');
  zh.classList.remove('hidden');
  grid.classList.remove('single');

  if (view === 'en') {
    zh.classList.add('hidden');
    grid.classList.add('single');
  } else if (view === 'zh') {
    en.classList.add('hidden');
    grid.classList.add('single');
  }

  document.querySelectorAll('.tabs button').forEach(btn => {
    btn.classList.toggle('active', btn.dataset.view === view);
  });
}
</script>
</body>
</html>
